{"source_slots":{"s2":"I'm thinking more about the structure of the piece itself, like how the parts interact. Maybe using a recurring motif or a central rhythm that everyone can follow, even if their individual lines are simpler. Would that help keep it cohesive?","s3":"That makes a lot of sense. A unifying rhythm or a consistent musical/structural motif is exactly what's needed to keep everything in sync, even if the individual contributions are different.

If you're looking to maintain cohesion while still having a mix of skill levels—what's the best approach? Focusing on a very strong central beat or motif that *everyone* can easily follow, regardless of their individual skill level.

Does focusing on that central, "universal" rhythm help your goal of keeping things cohesive?"}}
